From 5008602cb399a72a0ae413b3ff63e095e1461c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:51:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_tasks_panel: the Agent Tasks panel speaks pt-BR

The Agent Tasks panel (0035 and the patches since) reads its text through
zeo_i18n's t! from locales/<language>/agent-tasks.ftl, in en-US and pt-BR:
the filters and their tooltips, the filter input, the empty states, the
pages, the notices, the toolbar and selection actions, the delete prompt,
every row control and its aria label, the status and usage line, the
preview, the log tabs and the sub-thread rows. The en-US file is the code's
English byte for byte. The filters select on $filter, the status on $status;
the delete prompt's and the tool count's plurals are the messages'.

Kept as they are: the panel's name in the dock ("Agent Tasks", a name like
"Agent Sandbox"), "Waiting for you" (shared with Zed's subagent card), and the
English strings that are keys rather than text -- the filter buttons' element
ids and the sub-thread state behind its selector -- marked "i18n: not text".

At the end of the claude-agent-acp-plus group, after 0181.
---

